---
import LegalLayout from "../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { BRAND } from "@vc/config";
import { isMarketingHost } from "../../server/public-blog";
import { publicRuntimeEnv } from "../../server/runtime";

const env = publicRuntimeEnv(Astro);
if (env.selfHosted || !isMarketingHost(Astro.request, env)) {
  return new Response("Not found", {
    status: 404,
    headers: { "content-type": "text/plain; charset=utf-8" },
  });
}
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description={`The agreement for using ${BRAND.name} during public early access.`}
  updated="August 16, 2026"
>
  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>
    vibecms is a publishing platform and API operated by Ideaplexa LLC: one hosted blog, Markdown
    posts with version history, media storage, analytics, and scoped access for AI agents over
    MCP, REST, and a CLI. These terms apply to the hosted service. Self-hosting remains free and
    open under its own license.
  </p>

  <h2>Public early access</h2>
  <p>
    You are joining early. We work hard to keep the service stable, but features, limits, and
    quotas may change as the product matures. We will give reasonable notice before changes that
    could affect your published content.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account and tokens</h2>
  <p>
    Keep your sign-in email accessible and your API tokens secret. You are responsible for
    activity that happens through your tokens, including actions taken by AI agents you connect.
    Scope tokens narrowly and revoke any you no longer use.
  </p>

  <h2>Your content</h2>
  <p>
    You own your content. You grant us only the rights needed to host, serve, and back it up.
    You are responsible for the legality of what you publish and for having the rights to it.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No unlawful, deceptive, or rights-violating content.</li>
    <li>No malware distribution, spam infrastructure, or attempts to access other workspaces.</li>
    <li>Respect published API rate limits and quotas.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may suspend workspaces that violate these rules, and we will say why when we do.
  </p>

  <h2>Free and paid plans</h2>
  <p>
    Drafting, agent connection, and your first 5 published posts are free, with no card required.
    Publishing beyond that, media uploads, custom domains, and the full API surface require a
    subscription, billed in USD by Polar. Subscriptions renew automatically and you can cancel
    anytime; cancellation takes effect at the end of the paid period and unused time is not
    refunded except where required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Launch offer</h2>
  <p>
    Launch-offer prices are available to the first 100 subscribers across monthly and yearly
    billing and are applied automatically at checkout. While your subscription stays continuously
    active, your launch rate is locked: future list-price increases do not apply to you. If the
    subscription lapses, the launch rate ends and available-at-that-time pricing applies to a
    new subscription.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    The service is provided as is during early access. We target high availability but do not
    guarantee uninterrupted service, and we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses.
    In any case, our total liability is limited to the amounts you paid in the twelve months
    before the claim.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending things</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using vibecms anytime. Canceling a subscription switches the workspace off
    paid features at period end; your content remains exportable through the API, and we remove
    it on request.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:support@vibecms.dev">support@vibecms.dev</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
